record templartorrent.evidence.picker-microbench/1 : evidence {
    title "Same host, release, three runs at each of 1k, 100k and 1M pieces, full-bitfield peer. Reference pick p50 ns: 1k 2750/2760/2677; 100k 137038/154712/170449; 1M 1356235/1331665/1357768. Indexed pick p50 ns: 1k 42/40/40; 100k 952/927/819; 1M 7894/8232/7900, so 65x, 150x to 200x and about 170x below the reference within the same runs; p95 within 10 percent of p50. Sparse-peer path (one piece in sixteen) 205 to 223 ns, 11784 to 13920 ns and 164393 to 175714 ns. Maintenance the reference never paid: rank rebuild 6.2 us, 430 to 463 us and 4.8 to 5.1 ms; a whole-bitfield availability sweep 10 us, 810 to 834 us and 8.2 to 8.5 ms. About 12 bytes per piece plus bucket vectors. The reference at 1M measured 1.35 ms here against 4.8 ms in the morning baseline, so only within-run ratios are claimed."
    state verified
    result pass
    method command
    observed_at git:1a8d451aecf058c880b14445f215a5c52c7019f6
    command "cargo run --release -p templartorrent-bench -- --pieces 100000 --iterations 300"
    artifact "perf-results/2026-10-22-picker/microbench-100000-run1.jsonl"
    summary """
        Same host, release, three runs at each of 1k, 100k and 1M pieces, full-bitfield peer. Reference pick p50 ns: 1k 2750/2760/2677; 100k 137038/154712/170449; 1M 1356235/1331665/1357768. Indexed pick p50 ns: 1k 42/40/40; 100k 952/927/819; 1M 7894/8232/7900, so 65x, 150x to 200x and about 170x below the reference within the same runs; p95 within 10 percent of p50. Sparse-peer path (one piece in sixteen) 205 to 223 ns, 11784 to 13920 ns and 164393 to 175714 ns. Maintenance the reference never paid: rank rebuild 6.2 us, 430 to 463 us and 4.8 to 5.1 ms; a whole-bitfield availability sweep 10 us, 810 to 834 us and 8.2 to 8.5 ms. About 12 bytes per piece plus bucket vectors. The reference at 1M measured 1.35 ms here against 4.8 ms in the morning baseline, so only within-run ratios are claimed.
